# Coach speech (French): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "tu"; the player's gender is
# unknown: no adjective or participle agrees with the player ("tu gagnais", "tu progresses").
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   with their article ("l'ouverture", "le milieu de partie", "la finale"):
#                       never after "à" or "de" (no "au", "du"); "dans {text}", "{text} a été...".
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement after "Partie nulle, {text}." ("par répétition").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase ("regarder tout l'échiquier avant de jouer"), said
#                       after a colon or after "pense à".
#   appraisal.level.*   the coach page's level name in guillemets, said after "niveau":
#                       "au niveau {level}" = "au niveau « Débutant »".
# {opening:def} = the opening's name with its article ("la partie italienne", openings/fr.lang).
# Never "nulle" alone in speech (it sounds like "nul"): "partie nulle", "la nulle".
# Accuracy: "{acc} pour cent" (digits written, words spoken).

